Section 1. Short Title.
This Act may be cited as the ``Federal Agency Customer Experience Act''.

SEC. 2. FINDINGS.
Congress finds that--
(1) the Federal Government is the largest provider of goods and services in the United States, with an annual budget of over $4 trillion;
(2) the Federal Government is the largest employer in the United States, with over 2 million employees;
(3) the Federal Government interacts with the public in person, by mail, by telephone, and through digital channels;
(4) the Federal Government has a responsibility to provide excellent customer service to the public;
(5) the Federal Government must improve its customer service to better serve the public and to increase public trust in the Federal Government;
